##DESCRIPTION
##  Problem converts between decimal and base-5
##ENDDESCRIPTION

##KEYWORDS('teacher preparation', 'base-5')

## DBsubject('Arithmetic')
## DBchapter('Other Number Systems')
## DBsection('Base 5 Numbers')
## Date('8/30/2020')
## Author('Peter Staab')
## Institution('Fitchburg State University')

DOCUMENT();
loadMacros('PGstandard.pl', 'PGML.pl', 'contextBaseN.pl', 'PGcourse.pl');

Context('BaseN')->setBase(5);

$a1 = random(6,   24,  1);
$a2 = random(25,  124, 1);
$a3 = random(125, 625, 1);

$a1_5 = Real($a1);
$a2_5 = Real($a2);
$a3_5 = Real($a3);
BEGIN_PGML

Convert each of the following from decimal to base-5.

1. [`[$a1]`]=[__]*{$a1_5}

2. [`[$a2]`]=[__]*{$a2_5}

3. [`[$a3]`]=[__]*{$a3_5}

END_PGML

BEGIN_PGML_HINT
Think about using the chip/coin model.  Converting the number 17 to base 5 is
3 nickels and 2 pennies, so [`17 = 32_5`].

END_PGML_HINT

@d1 = split //, "$a1_5";
@d2 = split //, "$a2_5";
@d3 = split //, "$a3_5";

BEGIN_PGML_SOLUTION

We will solve this in an intuitive nature, thinking of determining the number of
pennies, nickels, quarters and 125-cent coins.

1. To convert [`[$a1]`] to base-5, note that since this is less than 25, it is a
2-digit base-5 number.  This can be written as [`[$d1[0]]`] nickels and [`[$d1[1]]`]
pennies so [`[$a1]`] in decimal is [`[$a1_5]_5`].

2. To convert [`[$a2]`] to base-5, note that since this is less than 125, it is a
3-digit base-5 number.  First, note that there are [`[$d2[0]]`] quarters in this number.
Then the remainder is [`[$a2]-[$d2[0]*25]=[$a2-$d2[0]*25]`].

    This can be written as [`[$d2[1]]`] nickels and [`[$d2[2]]`] pennies so [`[$a2]`]
    in decimal is [`[$a2_5]_5`].

3. To convert [`[$a3]`] to base-5, note that since this is more than 125 and less than 625,
so it is a 4-digit base-5 number.  First, note that there are [`[$d3[0]]`] 125s in this
number.  Then the remainder is [`[$a3]-[$d3[0]*125]=[$a3-$d3[0]*125]`].

    We then convert [`[$a3-$d3[0]*125]`] to base-5.  This has [`[$d3[1]]`] quarters in it
    with [`[$a3-$d3[0]*125]-[$d3[1]*25]=[$a3-$d3[0]*125-$d3[1]*25]`] leftover which is [`[$d3[2]]`] nickels and [`[$d3[3]]`] pennies.

    The result is that [`[$a3]`] in base-5 is [`[$a3_5]_5`].


END_PGML_SOLUTION

ENDDOCUMENT();
